<speak>I usually access it at home. In the office, the screen is always full of business messages, and I do not like switching between work and personal matters when staff are coming in and out. At home I use a tablet, which is easier on my eyes. The trouble is that the inbox looks slightly different from the one on the desktop, and I sometimes forget where the documents are. I can get there eventually, but it takes a few attempts. My daughter says I should stop tapping so quickly and actually read the headings. That is probably fair advice.</speak>